WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:01.480
Report

00:03.960 --> 00:04.880
Report

00:04.960 --> 00:06.240
The west gate has been breached

00:06.320 --> 00:09.320
That old thing Liu Dadao ran with his men

00:09.760 --> 00:11.160
Bastard

00:12.240 --> 00:13.160
You few

00:13.240 --> 00:14.907
Follow me to the west

00:24.560 --> 00:26.680
As many volunteers fled

00:26.880 --> 00:29.600
The west quickly lost its ability to resist

00:29.880 --> 00:32.547
The Wuzhao swarmed in through the west gate

00:33.200 --> 00:35.360
Even if you immediately send reinforcements

00:35.720 --> 00:38.360
The situation is already beyond saving

01:09.600 --> 01:11.000
Bring torches

01:13.000 --> 01:25.000
In the eleventh month of the 19th year of Yuankang, Yiyang fell. The Prince of Jin, Sikong Yao, set fire to the granaries and fought to the death, perishing from exhaustion on the battlefield.

01:34.000 --> 01:43.000
Shi Lang's host flooded into the city, plundering Yiyang for three days straight. Countless civilians perished, and Great Xuan's northern bastion was utterly reduced to ashes.

